{"step_index":119,"source":"MODEL","type":"PLANNER_RESPONSE","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-09-21T20:50:47Z","thinking":"The plan is to develop a module that analyzes dependency files, specifically Python's `requirements.txt` and Node.js's `package.json`. Its core function involves extracting package names alongside their version specifications. Further investigation will involve querying an online vulnerability database using the extracted package/version information to identify any known Common Vulnerabilities and Exposures (CVEs) that may be present. This module will handle network connectivity issues gracefully by logging them.\n\n\n","tool_calls":[{"name":"write_to_file","args":{"CodeContent":"\"\\\"\\\"\\\"\\nDependency Scanner for SmartAGENT.\\nParses dependency manifests (requirements.txt, package.json)\\nand queries the free Open Source Vulnerabilities (OSV.dev) database for known CVEs.\\n\\\"\\\"\\\"\\n\\nimport re\\nimport json\\nimport uuid\\nfrom typing import List, Dict, Any\\nimport requests\\n\\nfrom smartagent.scanners.base import BaseScanner, Finding\\n\\n\\nclass DependencyScanner(BaseScanner):\\n    def __init__(self):\\n        super().__init__(name=\\\"DependencyScanner\\\")\\n        self.osv_api_url = \\\"https://api.osv.dev/v1/query\\\"\\n\\n    def scan_file(self, file_path: str, content: str) -> List[Finding]:\\n        findings: List[Finding] = []\\n\\n        if file_path.endswith(\\\"requirements.txt\\\"):\\n            findings.extend(self._scan_python_requirements(file_path, content))\\n        elif file_path.endswith(\\\"package.json\\\"):\\n            findings.extend(self._scan_npm_package_json(file_path, content))\\n\\n        return findings\\n\\n    def _query_osv(self, package_name: str, version: str, ecosystem: str) -> List[Dict[str, Any]]:\\n        \\\"\\\"\\\"Query OSV API for known vulnerabilities.\\\"\\\"\\\"\\n        payload = {\\n            \\\"version\\\": version,\\n            \\\"package\\\": {\\n                \\\"name\\\": package_name,\\n                \\\"ecosystem\\\": ecosystem\\n            }\\n        }\\n        try:\\n            resp = requests.post(self.osv_api_url, json=payload, timeout=4)\\n            if resp.status_code == 200:\\n                data = resp.json()\\n                return data.get(\\\"vulns\\\", [])\\n        except Exception:\\n            # Silent fallback if offline or request blocked\\n            pass\\n        return []\\n\\n    def _scan_python_requirements(self, file_path: str, content: str) -> List[Finding]:\\n        findings: List[Finding] = []\\n        lines = content.splitlines()\\n\\n        for idx, line in enumerate(lines, start=1):\\n            line_clean = line.strip()\\n            if not line_clean or line_clean.startswith(\\\"#\\\"):\\n                continue\\n\\n            match = re.match(r\\\"^([a-zA-Z0-9_\\\\-\\\\.]+)\n<truncated 3026 bytes>","Description":"\"Create DependencyScanner for scanning requirements.txt and package.json via OSV.dev\"","Overwrite":"true","TargetFile":"\"c:\\\\Users\\\\k4ran\\\\OneDrive\\\\Desktop\\\\smartAGENT\\\\smartagent\\\\scanners\\\\dependency_scanner.py\"","toolAction":"\"Creating file\"","toolSummary":"\"Create smartagent/scanners/dependency_scanner.py\""}}],"truncated_fields":["tool_calls"]}
